Willing to relocate: Yes, within India &#x2F; Worldwide (would need assistance)<p>Technologies: Python, PyTorch, computer vision, deep learning, NLP Systems&#x2F;LLMs, Agentic AI, ONNX Runtime, C&#x2F;Go, TypeScript, SQL&#x2F;PostgreSQL, FastAPI, Next.js, ESP32&#x2F;FreeRTOS, Linux, Docker, CI&#x2F;CD<p>Résumé&#x2F;CV: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;rudraxd.in&#x2F;resume.pdf" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;rudraxd.in&#x2F;resume.pdf</a><p>Email: work@rudraxd.in<p>Website: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;rudraxd.in" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;rudraxd.in</a> ;
GitHub: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;FireHead90544" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;FireHead90544</a> ;
LinkedIn: <a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.linkedin.com&#x2F;in&#x2F;rudraxd&#x2F;" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.linkedin.com&#x2F;in&#x2F;rudraxd&#x2F;</a><p>I&#x27;m a recent (2026) AI&#x2F;ML graduate, but most of my learning has come from building things that have to work outside a notebook. Having ~3 years of production experience and been into the programming&#x2F;cs domain for ~7 years.<p>At MiyuLabs, my small hardware&#x2F;software venture, I&#x27;ve built an ESP32-based interactive desk companion from firmware and device communication through the Go backend, database, deployment, and website. I&#x27;ve also built self-hosted email infrastructure with durable state, retries, rate limiting, and crash recovery. I enjoy owning the whole problem rather than handing off everything outside my immediate specialty.<p>On the ML side, I built a computer-vision quality-assessment pipeline using a custom YOLO segmentation model, reaching ~0.93 mAP50-95 on held-out data. That work included inference optimization and the surrounding application&#x2F;API pipeline, not just model training. Other projects include EFNet, a compact CNN–ViT hybrid for few-shot open-set retraining-free face recognition for edge devices; MooNet, an offline-first lightweight cattle-breed classifier; and RLSwarm, a multi-agent reinforcement-learning environment with experiments comparing PPO and DQN across swarm intelligence behaviours.<p>I&#x27;m looking for ML&#x2F;Applied AI, computer-vision&#x2F;NLP, ML systems, or backend&#x2F;distributed-systems engineering roles, especially on small teams where engineers are expected to investigate ambiguous problems, make pragmatic architecture decisions, and ship. I&#x27;m early-career by years, not claiming seniority I haven&#x27;t earned, but I bring a broad, hands-on engineering background (breadth-wise) and a strong bias toward building and measuring real systems (depth-wise).
